the the role of the dice is uh forcing you to move&nbsp;
the rook. And um there's another interesting thing&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:54.600 --> 00:11:59.720
I discovered about chess, which is it wasn't&nbsp;
a 2-player game originally but 4-player&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:59.720 --> 00:12:07.800
game. And actually you can see that um in the game that&nbsp;
survived, because your army consists of two knights,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:07.800 --> 00:12:13.640
two bishops, two rooks and the point is that you&nbsp;
actually captured one of the other players armies&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:13.640 --> 00:12:19.643
and it became part of your your army and that's&nbsp;
why you see these doubling up of pieces in the&nbsp;game.

